# gitleaks false positives — no real credentials in this repository.
#
# Every entry matches a known-fake test/CI fixture: an intentionally-dummy
# 32-byte lowercase-hex value, or a synthetic HMAC key, used only to exercise
# session-secret, signing-key and DPoP nonce handling.
#
# Format is gitleaks' own finding fingerprint, split on ':':
#   file:rule-id:start-line             matches in any commit
#   commit:file:rule-id:start-line      matches that revision only
# The last field MUST be the real 1-based start line from the scan output, and
# `rule-id` contains hyphens, so only split fields from the left. A wildcard
# there matches nothing and silently disables the entry. Entries are pinned to
# whole commit ids and to the revisions that report a finding, so a different
# commit using the same fixture under a moved line is reported rather than
# silently hidden.
#
# Added 2026-11-15 as part of Phase 1 security-tooling parity; repinned to real
# line numbers 2026-11-21 after wildcard entries were found to be inert.

